WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.140
 I like to break down
the DNA of a song,

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.460
to show you where it came from.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.220
In the case of "Nice
for What", Drake

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.970
sampling Lauryn Hill, when
Lauryn Hill is sampling

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:16.020
Wu-Tang Clan, which is Gladys
Knight covering a Barbra

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.370
Streisand song.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.750
It's a meta rabbit hole.

00:00:21.472 --> 00:00:23.430
Sometimes, you got to
let people in on the fun,

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.640
and there's nothing more
fun than the discovery of,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.900
"Oh, I know that song.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.190
That's where that comes from?"

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.920
To be honest with
you, not drumming

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.610
in the world's funkiest
group, not the book writing,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.440
not being on late
night television--

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.390
my first love is records.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.070
I've been listening
and analyzing

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.550
records since the age of five.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:46.290
I've never shared the method
to my madness or my secrets

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.880
or my creative process
in DJing until right now.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.660
In my MasterClass,
I will teach you

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.120
how to curate the
perfect playlist, how

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.090
to search for music, how to
figure out where it belongs.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.490
And then, I want to teach
you how to utilize it,

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.770
by being an effective DJ.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.230
So if I decide I need
an extra kick drum,

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:11.698
I can press when the kick
drum occurs, like right here.

00:01:11.698 --> 00:01:13.450
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.020
If you have any
relationship with music,

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.280
this class is for you.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.310
[BEATS DRUM RHYTHM]

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.130
That sort of rhythm
has not failed me yet.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.030
It's rhythmic.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.080
It's sexy.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.550
It makes everyone want to get on
the dance floor and just party.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.280
You can scratch.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:31.780
You can mix.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:32.280
You can cut.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.430
You can beat juggle.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.550
Take these tools and build
something of your own.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:40.720
Loving music and learning
how to find it and appreciate

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.588
it and use it to
find effect, that's

00:01:42.588 --> 00:01:43.630
what I want to teach you.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:51.830
I'm Questlove, and
this is my MasterClass.

